    "Description": "Migration slice 2 (docs/blueprints/ReverseToBaseline_Slice_Design.md): blueprint-authored rebuild of the C# oracle HillAttackTankNodes.Action_ReverseToBaseline (~line 456) -- an AiPrimitive BTreeAction. Graph: EventEntry -\u003E ChannelCommand(LocomotionChannel/MoveTo) [explicit data-in pins Destination/Speed/ArrivalRadius/ReverseAllowed; Destination wired from a pure FunctionCall VectorOps.Vec3(GetParameter(BaselineX), GetParameter(BaselineY), Literal 0f); Speed/ArrivalRadius/ReverseAllowed baked via PinDefaults] -\u003E WaitForChannel(LocomotionChannel) [AiPrimitive latent lowering: issues the command once, suspends: Running while channel Running, auto-Failure on channel Failure, continues to Out on channel Success] -\u003E PublishEvent(ClearBehaviorEvent, Target pin left unwired =\u003E self-default, Entity=self) -\u003E Return(Success). Q#13 UPDATE (deviation removed): WaitForChannel\u0027s OnFailure exec-out is now wired to PublishEvent(ClearBehaviorEvent) -\u003E Return(Failure), so the blueprint publishes ClearBehaviorEvent on BOTH the Success and Failure paths, exactly matching the C# oracle. (Previously the failure path auto-returned Failure without publishing -- the accepted simplification once documented in design doc \u00A72, now resolved by the Q#13 failure split.) New curated helper: Hrot.AI.Behaviors.Brains.VectorOps.Vec3/Vec2 (reflection-free Vector3 construction; no vector-literal node exists). Does not modify the C# oracle.",
